  "biobricks:reviewNotes": "Determined by Claude annotation agent. The repository name ontox_bayer suggests an intent to build a brick from Bayer-contributed data associated with the EU ONTOX project, but the brick was never actually populated: the download stage has an empty ftpbase, the dvc.lock is the unmodified brick-template example (data/mtcars.parquet), and the GitHub README/history (single \"Initial commit\") is the plain brick template. There is no upstream URL, no data, and no license statement anywhere in the repo. Recorded as UNSTATED / unknown. HUMAN MUST CHECK: whether a real ONTOX/Bayer source was ever intended and, if so, its access terms (ONTOX data and Bayer proprietary data may be controlled-access or restricted); this brick may simply be an abandoned/empty template that should be excluded from the catalog.",
